.TH MONO 2
.SH NAME
mono: aeadlock, aeadunlock, blake2b, x25519, edkeypair, edsign, edcheck, equal, version \- Monocypher cryptography
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "mono.m";
mono := load Mono Mono->PATH;

aeadlock:   fn(key, nonce, ad, plain: array of byte):
                (array of byte, array of byte);
aeadunlock: fn(key, nonce, tag, ad, cipher: array of byte): array of byte;
blake2b:    fn(msg, key: array of byte, n: int): array of byte;
x25519:     fn(sk, pk: array of byte): array of byte;
xpublic:    fn(sk: array of byte): array of byte;
edkeypair:  fn(seed: array of byte): (array of byte, array of byte);
edsign:     fn(sk, msg: array of byte): array of byte;
edcheck:    fn(sig, pk, msg: array of byte): int;
equal:      fn(a, b: array of byte): int;
version:    fn(): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mono
exposes
.B Monocypher
version 4.0.2 to Dis: XChaCha20-Poly1305, BLAKE2b, X25519 and EdDSA.
It is a builtin module, like
.IR Crypt ,
so it is available in the native kernel and in
.IR emu .
Arguments and results are copies; no pointer into the interpreter heap is
passed to the C library.
.PP
.B aeadlock
encrypts
.I plain
with
.I key
(32 bytes) and
.I nonce
(24 bytes), authenticating
.I ad
(which may be nil), and returns the ciphertext and a 16-byte tag.
.B aeadunlock
returns the plaintext, or
.B nil
if the tag does not verify (a wrong tag, key, nonce or associated data
all produce
.BR nil ,
not an error).
.PP
.B blake2b
hashes
.I msg
to
.I n
bytes, 1 to 64.  When
.I key
is non-nil (at most 64 bytes) the keyed variant is used.
.PP
.B x25519
multiplies the 32-byte scalar
.I sk
by the 32-byte point
.IR pk .
.B xpublic
returns the public key for
.I sk
(the base point is built into the library; do not construct one by
hand, because a fresh Limbo array is not guaranteed to be zeroed).
.PP
.B edkeypair
takes a 32-byte
.I seed
and returns a 64-byte secret key and a 32-byte public key.
.B edsign
signs with the secret key and returns 64 bytes;
.B edcheck
returns 1 if the signature is good and 0 otherwise.
.PP
.B equal
compares two arrays in constant time (for tags and keys).
.B version
returns the Monocypher version string.
.SH EXAMPLES
Encrypt and authenticate a message:
.IP
.EX
(ct, tag) := mono->aeadlock(key, nonce, ad, plain);
if(mono->aeadunlock(key, nonce, tag, ad, ct) == nil)
	raise "fail:tampered";
.EE
.PP
Key agreement:
.IP
.EX
mine := mono->x25519(mysk, theirpk);
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/mono.m
.br
.B /libinterp/mono.c
.br
.B /libsec/port/monocypher.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR crypt (2),
.IR keyring (2),
.IR certify (8),
.IR monotest (1)
.SH BUGS
EdDSA is Monocypher's BLAKE2b-based variant, not the SHA-512 construction
of RFC 8032, so RFC 8032 test vectors do not apply and signatures are not
interchangeable with other Ed25519 implementations.
.PP
The library arrived from the Plan 9 port in
.BR factotum-libtab .
Three source changes were needed for Inferno's
.IR 8c :
the ACSL comment inside the
.B FOR_T
macro was dropped, the Poly1305 block multiplication is written as
separate statements because
.I 8c
aborts in its 64-bit register allocator on the original expression, and
64-bit constants carry a
.B ULL
suffix, which
.I 8c
requires.
